{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479095-scent-the-divine-with-new-pantheons","id":1479095,"title":"Scent the divine with new pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-18T11:50:16-07:00","id":1479095,"title":"Scent the divine with new pantheons","content":"So, with the scion Dragon, Mythos and Demigod books coming out (relatively) soon, we have five new pantheons, dragons, and weird lovecraftian biz that are getting added to the game. Is there word anywhere in the books that I missed on what their scents would be to someone with the Scent the Divine knack? If nothing else a quick find search on Dragon's manuscript just mentions them eventually getting scent the divine but nothing about what they would smell like if anything. Also, does Scent the Divine work on pre-visitation scions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","user":"Storyteller323","date":". 04-18-2022, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T22:06:08-07:00","id":1482058,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to look into this for Masks of the Mythos specifically, and as far as I can tell it just doesn't exist in that book - unless I missed a more recent version, there just is not a Scent the Divine, a set of Virtues, or pantheon skills for the Mythos pantheon. Which is frustrating, since one would think that's very necessary for even being able to build a Mythos scion to begin with, and start incorporating them into your games before the final version comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24151-kingofferrets","name":"kingofferrets","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T02:22:30-07:00","id":1482064,"title":"","content":"With the Lovecraft Mythos it could be that they are simply to alien and divorced from mortal life to make Virtues work in human terms. As for scent the Divine, the stimuli would probably make no sense to three dimensional beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T02:50:40-07:00","id":1482065,"title":"","content":"On the Virtues thing, the Ready-Made Characters have a Virtues bar; so one would assume that the Mythos has Virtues with enough detail that the Storyguide can judge whether an action land toward one Virtue or the other. <br /> <br /> But yeah; the manuscript doesn't say anything more about them. That <i>does</i> seem like a rather big oversight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T04:50:03-07:00","id":1482067,"title":"","content":"I believe they've said there will be Virtues in the book. They were left out of the KS manuscript.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T11:21:43-07:00","id":1482180,"title":"","content":"The Mythos as smells/sensations that don't exist on Earth, instead being only found in the Dreamlands, on alien planets, or amongst the darkness between the stars. Or if that in too esoteric, perhaps the smells of fungi, rats, ozone, or death, all with a strong feeling of &quot;wrongness&quot;.<br /> <br /> For the Mesopotamians, maybe ancient sand/brick, wet clay, and exotic flora evoking the Hanging Gardens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T14:58:35-07:00","id":1482198,"title":"","content":"For the Mesopotamians the smell of farmland and the river and the sounds of the marketplace. These would have been their world. And still would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}